  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with PCA (config_001) achieves 0.485 accuracy, while image-only with ResNet50 (config_010) is very weak at 0.208, confirming RNA is the dominant signal. Uncertainty: We don't yet know whether a learned RNA representation (scvi) can improve upon the linear PCA_n2000 baseline. This experiment (config_004: rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200) isolates the effect of the RNA encoder by changing only that one variable relative to config_001. If scvi_n200 substantially outperforms PCA, it opens up many promising multimodal and multiprofile configurations; if it underperforms, it suggests PCA is already near the representation ceiling and we should focus on profile/aggregation/fusion choices instead. With 7 experiments remaining, resolving the representation question early maximizes the information value of subsequent experiments."
}

